# 5. AI STATUS SYSTEM

Create a visible AI status indicator.

The indicator must reflect actual functionality.

Use the following states:

### ONLINE AI AVAILABLE

The device has internet connectivity and the online AI service is reachable.

### OFFLINE AI READY

The device has no internet connectivity, but the local knowledge base is available and the local model is ready if installed.

### LOCAL KNOWLEDGE MODE

The user can ask questions and receive answers from the stored agricultural knowledge base, but a local generative model is not available.

### DOWNLOADING AI MODEL

The user has requested a local model download.

Show actual progress where the technology supports it.

### AI MODEL NOT INSTALLED

The user can still access the offline knowledge base.

Provide a clear option to download the model when connectivity is available.

### CONNECTION LOST

If the connection disappears during a conversation, automatically switch to local retrieval when possible.

Do not erase the user's question.

Do not make the user restart the conversation.

Do not display misleading status messages.

The status should update based on real connectivity, model readiness, and service availability.

